; hierarchy.dta — object hierarchy / roster probe.
;
; Widest-scope probe: every object in the directory, with its class, DTA type,
; owning dir and transform parent. This is the probe that answers "is the same
; set of objects even present on both sides, and are they wired to the same
; parents".
;
; Verified against the native port (dc3-native, HTTP debug server) 2026-08.
;   {$o class_name}      -> Hmx::Object HANDLE_EXPR(class_name)  Object.cpp:144
;   {$o dir}             -> Hmx::Object HANDLE_EXPR(dir)         Object.cpp:149
;   {$o get (type)}      -> Hmx::Object SYNC_PROP_SET(type)      Object.cpp:167
;   {$o get (trans_parent)} -> RndTransformable SYNC_PROP_SET    Trans.cpp:99
;
; `trans_parent` is guarded by `has`, so non-transformable objects report
; <absent> rather than a misleading <null>.

(probe hierarchy
    (doc "Every object in a dir: class, DTA type, owning dir, transform parent.")
    (discriminates
        "objects missing entirely on one side; proxy/inline dirs that failed to load; reparenting bugs; wrong object class for a name")
    (scope
        (dir main)
        (limit 4000))
    (fields
        (class        msg  class_name      sym)
        (type         prop (type)          sym)
        (owner_dir    msg  dir             obj)
        (trans_parent prop (trans_parent)  obj)))
